  "findings": [
    "One large model worker observed throughout; both concurrent requests reused the same model.",
    "The operation lock serialized inference. Job 1 began only after job 2 completed its inference.",
    "Concurrent requests did not double the model memory footprint.",
    "A pending job may show phase=running while progress.stage=queued; this is a current status-display limitation.",
    "Independent output directories are required for distinct concurrent tasks; active-job deduplication currently keys on output directory."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "One public image repeated into fresh output directories; no business-cache hits.",
    "First business request was slower. No statistical throughput or broad accuracy claim.",
    "Only two live concurrent requests were tested. The 8-job cap was checked with a simulated executor.",
    "Windows memory readings sampled every 0.5s; working set and private bytes are different measures.",
    "Two independent loaded model instances were not tested. Memory pressure and slowdown are inferred risks, not measured outcomes.",
    "No process was forcibly stopped by the benchmark; model remains resident."
  ],
